# Pantheon holds a hash-indexed copy of conversations and seat state. Per docs/specs §6.2, that
# material stays inside $PANTHEON_HOME, is never committed, and never leaves the machine.
# This file is the mechanical form of that promise — deny by default, allow deliberately.
*

!/.gitignore
!/README.md
# Codex reads this one. Per the AGENTS.md spec it is purely instructional -- it cannot define an
# agent -- and Codex concatenates from the repo root downward under a 32 KiB project_doc_max_bytes
# cap, so keep it short enough that a nested file would still fit beneath it.
!/AGENTS.md
!/docs/
!/docs/**
!/spike/
!/spike/**
!/bin/
!/bin/**
!/src/
!/src/**
!/tests/
!/tests/**
!/package.json
!/STATE.md
!/scripts/
!/scripts/**
# A declared dependency without a lockfile is an unpinned supply chain. The zero-runtime-dep
# policy that made a lockfile pointless ended when SDK transport was adopted; pinning the tree
# is the replacement control, not an exception to the old one.
!/package-lock.json

# Role cards for the orchestrated roles. The directory is un-ignored, its contents re-ignored, and
# only agents/ allowed back in -- git cannot re-include a child of an excluded parent, so the three
# lines have to be in this order. Nothing else under .claude/ is tracked.
!/.claude/
/.claude/*
!/.claude/agents/
!/.claude/agents/**

# The same shape for the Antigravity CLI's customization root: only its custom agents (the role cards
# the agy seat loads on both lanes) are tracked; skills, rules, hooks or anything else it may write there
# stay ignored until admitted deliberately.
!/.agents/
/.agents/*
!/.agents/agents/
!/.agents/agents/**

# …and never these, even if a rule above would otherwise admit them.
/.pantheon/
**/artifacts/
**/*.jsonl

# ONE deliberate exception to the .jsonl rule above, and it has to come after it because the last
# matching rule wins. `docs/runs/graph/` is the build-correction graph: hand-authored source that
# scripts/graph-check.mjs validates and renders, not a receipt, a transcript or a progress stream.
# Everything the blanket rule is protecting against (run progress, seat transcripts, spend records)
# lives under outputs/ or $PANTHEON_HOME and stays ignored.
!/docs/runs/graph/*.jsonl
**/transcripts/
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite-*
.env
.env.*
